<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Aulerci Cenomani</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Vindinum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Maine, centred on Le Mans, a branch of whom crossed the Alps and founded the Celtic towns of Brescia and Verona.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cenomani">Cenomani</a> were the largest branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulerci">Aulerci</a> and held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarthe">Sarthe</a> valley around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-mans">Vindinum</a> (Le Mans). <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> report that part of the people migrated across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> around 400 BCE and settled north of the Po, where the Italian Cenomani founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brixia</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a>) and became allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> against the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gauls</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of the Gallic <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cenomani">Cenomani</a> at home. They struck gold coins and controlled the route between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">Channel</a> coast.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They joined the great revolt of 52 BCE and sent five thousand men to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-mans">Vindinum</a> grew into a walled town, later called Civitas Cenomanorum, from which come the names Le Mans and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-maine">Maine</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/aulerci-cenomani.jpg" alt="Aulerci Cenomani" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Cénomans (peuple celtique de Gaule). Autorité émettrice de monnaie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Stat%C3%A8re,_or,_fonds_celtique,_C%C3%A9nomans_-_btv1b11289132j_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vindinum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cenomani</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=aulerci-cenomani" aria-label="Aulerci Cenomani on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4729 535 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aulerci Cenomani lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5049 791h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5049 791h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=aulerci-cenomani">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

